class:: SpecFlatness2
summary:: Stable spectral flatness with explicit conventions
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/SpecFlatness

description::
Returns the geometric mean divided by the arithmetic mean of nonnegative spectral weights. Values approach 0 for concentrated spectra and 1 for uniform spectra. The logarithmic floor stabilizes individual bins, while an all-silent frame returns exactly 0.

The analyzer reads FFT values without changing them. It is practically similar to link::Classes/SpecFlatness::, but documents magnitude/power selection, frequency limits, floor, update policy, and silence behavior.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain produced with the same literal size as code::fftSize::.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 uses magnitude and 1 uses power.

argument:: floor
Positive logarithmic floor applied before the geometric mean.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
A ratio from 0 through 1.

instancemethods::

examples::
Spectral flatness measures the ratio of geometric to arithmetic mean of the spectrum. In this example, flatness dynamically crossfades between a pitched resonant drone (when the sound has tonal peaks) and a wide granular white noise diffuser (when the sound is noisy and flat). An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: monitors flatness in real time.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("texture.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic texture fallback
            PinkNoise.ar * LFNoise1.kr(1).range(0.2, 0.8) + SinOsc.ar(LFNoise0.kr(2).range(200, 800), 0, 0.2)
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        var flatness = SpecFlatness2.kr(chain, minFreq: 100, maxFreq: 12000, fftSize: 1024);
        var flatSmooth = flatness.lag(0.05);

        // Resonant pitched drone (favored on low flatness / tonal content)
        var drone = BPF.ar(Saw.ar([110, 220, 330]), 220, 0.1).sum * (1.0 - flatSmooth);
        // Diffuse noise texture (favored on high flatness / stochastic content)
        var diffuser = Dust2.ar(2000) * flatSmooth * 0.4;
        var sound = (source * 0.2) + (drone * 0.25) + (diffuser * 0.2);

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, flatness) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2) ! 2
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Spectral Flatness", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

